## Usability Discussion
Accounting for beam deformation improves the realism and reliability of the nutcracker design. By limiting deflection to less than 2% of the handle length, the system 
ensures that most of the input force is effectively transmitted to the nut rather than lost through structural bending. The use of a hollow aluminum beam provides a high 
stiffness-to-weight ratio, allowing the handles to remain lightweight while still resisting deformation. This improves handling and reduces unnecessary material usage.
Replacing manual input with a linear actuator allows for more consistent and controlled force application. This enhances usability by making the nutcracker easier to 
operate, more repeatable in performance, and less dependent on user strength.

